# API Contracts Version Alignment

RULE: Interfaces and services that depend on api-contracts must run `check_sdk_version_alignment.py` in quality gates. If an interface uses an SDK (databento, ccxt, ib_insync, tardis-client), its version must align with api-contracts [schema-validation].
WHY: Prevents schema drift; ensures interfaces validate against correct schema versions.
CODEX: 02-data/schema-governance.md, 05-infrastructure/unified-libraries/dependency-matrix.md

DO:
  Add SDK alignment step to quality-gates.sh
  Use `--interface-path .` when running from interface repo (e.g. unified-market-interface)
  Run from api-contracts: `python scripts/check_sdk_version_alignment.py`
  Run from interface: `python ../api-contracts/scripts/check_sdk_version_alignment.py --interface-path .`

NEVER:
  Skip version alignment in interfaces that use api-contracts + SDK deps
  Use SDK version not pinned in api-contracts [schema-validation]
  Add new SDK dep to interface without adding to api-contracts schema-validation first

See also: `api-contracts-usage.mdc`, `path-dependency-ci.mdc`, `dependency-version-alignment.mdc`.
